{#- v3 image macros (WS6, engineering 3.9). Import:
      {% from "v3/media.njk" import picture, preload %}

    picture(item, sizes, opts)
      item   one entry of _data/images.json, for example images["storefront-hero"]:
             { width, height, fallback, avif, webp, jpeg, alt, pos, phone? } where avif, webp and
             jpeg are srcset strings. Two other shapes are accepted:
               art directed   item.phone = { avif, webp, jpeg, sizes, aspect, width, height }, a
                              different crop served below 1024px (change with opts.phoneMedia)
               CMS upload     { cdn: true, src: "/images/uploads/x.jpg", width, height, alt }:
                              AVIF and WebP come through Netlify Image CDN with explicit fm=
                              (the CDN prefers WebP when fm is left out), the JPEG original is the
                              <img>. Never mix both pipelines on one image.
      sizes  the honest sizes attribute for the desktop crop, for example "(min-width: 1024px) 50vw, 100vw"
      opts   { alt, decorative, high, eager, cls, phoneMedia, phoneSizes }
             alt         required (or item.alt). The build stops with a named error without it, or
                         when it carries an em dash, an en dash or an emoji
             decorative  true prints alt="" on purpose (no error)
             high        true = above-the-fold hero: fetchpriority="high", no loading attribute
             eager       true = no lazy loading (without high)
             cls         class for the <img>
    Output: <picture> with AVIF then WebP <source> elements (phone sources first when art directed),
    then an <img> with src (JPEG 960), srcset, sizes, width, height, alt, decoding="async" and
    loading="lazy" unless high or eager. An art directed img carries data-art and the two aspect ratios as
    custom properties (80-media.css turns them into aspect-ratio per breakpoint, so the box is
    reserved at the right shape and nothing shifts). object-position comes from the data focal point, so a
    CSS object-fit: cover box keeps the subject in view.

    preload(item, sizes)
      the one hero preload per page: <link rel="preload" as="image" type="image/avif" imagesrcset
      imagesizes fetchpriority="high"> where imagesizes equals the <img> sizes. For an art directed
      item it prints two links, one per media query (the browser fetches only the one that matches),
      so the phone crop is preloaded on phones and the desktop crop on desktops. -#}
{% macro picture(item, sizes, opts) -%}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
{%- set altText = item | picAlt(o) -%}
{%- set sz = sizes or "100vw" -%}
{%- set ph = item.phone -%}
{%- set pm = o.phoneMedia or "(max-width: 1023px)" -%}
{%- set pz = o.phoneSizes or (ph.sizes if ph else "100vw") -%}
{%- if item.cdn -%}
{%- set avifSet = item.src | cdnSet("avif", item.width) -%}
{%- set webpSet = item.src | cdnSet("webp", item.width) -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set avifSet = item.avif -%}
{%- set webpSet = item.webp -%}
{%- endif -%}
<picture>
{%- if ph %}
<source media="{{ pm }}" type="image/avif" srcset="{{ ph.avif }}" sizes="{{ pz }}">
<source media="{{ pm }}" type="image/webp" srcset="{{ ph.webp }}" sizes="{{ pz }}">
<source media="{{ pm }}" srcset="{{ ph.jpeg }}" sizes="{{ pz }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- if avifSet %}
<source type="image/avif" srcset="{{ avifSet }}" sizes="{{ sz }}">
{%- endif %}
{%- if webpSet %}
<source type="image/webp" srcset="{{ webpSet }}" sizes="{{ sz }}">
{%- endif %}
<img{% if o.cls %} class="{{ o.cls }}"{% endif %} src="{{ item.src if item.cdn else item.fallback }}"{% if item.jpeg and not item.cdn %} srcset="{{ item.jpeg }}" sizes="{{ sz }}"{% endif %} width="{{ item.width }}" height="{{ item.height }}" alt="{{ altText }}"{% if ph %} data-art style="{% if item.pos %}object-position:{{ item.pos }};{% endif %}--ar-d:{{ item.width }}/{{ item.height }};--ar-m:{{ ph.width }}/{{ ph.height }}"{% elif item.pos %} style="object-position:{{ item.pos }}"{% endif %}{% if o.high %} fetchpriority="high"{% elif not o.eager %} loading="lazy"{% endif %} decoding="async">
</picture>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro preload(item, sizes) -%}
{%- if item and item.avif -%}
{%- if item.phone -%}
<link rel="preload" as="image" type="image/avif" media="(max-width: 1023px)" imagesrcset="{{ item.phone.avif }}" imagesizes="{{ item.phone.sizes or '100vw' }}" fetchpriority="high">
<link rel="preload" as="image" type="image/avif" media="(min-width: 1024px)" imagesrcset="{{ item.avif }}" imagesizes="{{ sizes or '100vw' }}" fetchpriority="high">
{%- else -%}
<link rel="preload" as="image" type="image/avif" imagesrcset="{{ item.avif }}" imagesizes="{{ sizes or '100vw' }}" fetchpriority="high">
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
